    "modified": "2026-10-07",
    "opening": "Your photography business profit margin is the month's profit divided by the month's net sales, using a clearly stated cost boundary. In the fictional portrait month below, $5,000 sales leave $850 after variable costs, overhead and the owner's income goal: a 17% planning margin. That is different from a session's contribution percentage. Measure the actual service mix and complete editing workload before comparing margins. These USD figures are examples, not industry averages or a forecast of bookings.",
